-- title:
--   Chart points are not w-translates under comaximality
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a non-zero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model datum of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, whose field `w` provides an automorphism of the model $X$ of level $\Gamma_M(M,H)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(R p)$. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` for the finite chart algebra, the subalgebra of integral elements of the function field over the $R p$-subalgebra generated by the $j$-coordinate, and $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ for the associated open immersion $\operatorname{Spec} A \to X$. Let $\vartheta$ be an $R p$-algebra automorphism of $A$ reading `w` on this chart, in the sense that $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ followed by `𝔛.w.hom` equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\vartheta)$ followed by $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$. Let $a, b \in A$ satisfy $(b) + (\vartheta a) = A$, and let $\mathfrak{q}, \mathfrak{q}'$ be prime ideals of $A$ with $a \in \mathfrak{q}$ and $b \in \mathfrak{q}'$. Then the image of $\mathfrak{q}$ under $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ differs from the image of $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathfrak{q}')$ under `𝔛.w.hom`.
--
--   This is a geometric disjointness step for the Atkin–Lehner type automorphism `w` of the model of $X_H$ at $p$: it separates a point of the finite chart from the $w$-translate of another whenever suitable chart functions are comaximal. It is used in the construction of one-sided pools of points after base change, via [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_oneSidedPool_baseChange_of_levelPolynomials`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_oneSidedPool_baseChange_of_levelPolynomials).
